00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:42.460
Creed has a light tan baseball hat.

504
00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:44.640
Ryan has a white visor.

505
00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:47.320
Stanley has a straw sun hat.

506
00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:53.440
Phyllis has no hat while she's playing volleyball, but she has a straw sun hat on the sidelines.

507
00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:55.240
Meredith has no hat.

508
00:23:55.740 --> 00:23:57.280
Oscar has no hat.

509
00:23:58.020 --> 00:24:02.660
Charles Minor has a black Nike visor.

510
00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:04.120
How did we get away with that?

511
00:24:04.120 --> 00:24:05.200
I don't know!

512
00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:06.100
Because it's Idris.

513
00:24:06.320 --> 00:24:08.800
And we're just like, let Idris do what he wants to do.

514
00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:10.580
We're just glad to have you back.

515
00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:11.640
I don't know.

516
00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:15.780
Toby also has a yellow baseball hat with a logo.

517
00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:18.520
It has little trees, but I couldn't read what it was.

518
00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:22.860
Well, you know, part of the hat strategy was because it got so hot during the day.

519
00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.080
We needed it.

520
00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:32.620
We needed it when we were playing volleyball as well to kind of create a shade on our faces so that you could see our expressions.

521
00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:36.800
So we weren't completely blown out by the sun, also for sun protection.

522
00:24:37.240 --> 00:24:40.520
But you might notice that Michael and Holly do not wear hats.

523
00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:45.260
They are mostly in their cutesy little, like, love neSt.

524
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:46.180
Shady tree area.

525
00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:47.280
Yeah, exactly.

526
00:24:47.660 --> 00:24:49.580
Well, Jenna, I also did a little bit of tracking.

527
00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:55.380
I want you to know that I feel like this episode really brings out some of our characters' other traits.

528
00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:57.300
Oh, I made a liSt.

529
00:24:57.560 --> 00:25:10.880
We have Sporty Pam, Saucy Jim, Petty Charles, Trash Talking Andy, Snarky Michael, and my most favorite, Vacation Stanley.

530
00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:13.560
I love Vacation Stanley.

531
00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:16.920
So the picnic starts with Pam and Jim.

532
00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:22.940
They're walking up, and they share a little bit about what last year's softball company picnic was like.

533
00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:27.100
Jim had that spider in his mitt, but that's not what Pam is talking about.

534
00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:31.180
She's talking about the guy who grabbed her boobs to keep his balance.

535
00:25:31.740 --> 00:25:32.420
Uh-huh.

536
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:37.500
And then Pam points at her chest and says, yeah, you don't grab these for balance.

537
00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:39.540
And Jim goes, well.

538
00:25:39.900 --> 00:25:41.860
And this is Saucy Jim.

539
00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:48.540
Well, next up, Dwight arrives with his friend, Rolf.

540
00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:50.200
His best friend.

541
00:25:50.200 --> 00:25:58.460
And who they met at a shoe store when Dwight overheard Rolf asking for a shoe that would increase his speed but not leave any tracks.

542
00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:00.220
These two are made for each other.

543
00:26:00.580 --> 00:26:02.700
We had a fan question from David H.

544
00:26:02.820 --> 00:26:03.440
in Pennsylvania.

545
00:26:03.700 --> 00:26:05.160
Who played Dwight's friend?

546
00:26:05.460 --> 00:26:07.760
Was he somehow related to the show already?

547
00:26:08.220 --> 00:26:12.280
Guys, Rolf was played by the amazing James Urbaniac.

548
00:26:12.580 --> 00:26:13.600
And get this, Ange.

549
00:26:13.680 --> 00:26:13.920
What?

550
00:26:14.160 --> 00:26:17.600
He auditioned and was called back for the role of Dwight.

551
00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:20.200
Well, that makes perfect sense to me.

552
00:26:20.440 --> 00:26:20.780
Doesn't it?

553
00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:24.040
He and Rain knew each other from their New York theater days.

554
00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:29.360
And after Rain read this script, he called James and gave him a heads up.

555
00:26:30.040 --> 00:26:33.420
And he told Greg, you need to bring in James Urbaniac for this.

556
00:26:33.520 --> 00:26:35.540
Well, they knew him because they had auditioned him.

557
00:26:35.740 --> 00:26:37.660
So he went in to see Allison Jones.

558
00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:39.120
He read for the role.

559
00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:49.260
Ken talked a little bit in the DVD commentary about just how perfectly cast James was and that for a guest star to come in on such a big episode,

560
00:26:49.880 --> 00:26:54.020
James just fit in so seamlessly you would have never known he had never been on the show before.

561
00:26:54.220 --> 00:26:59.020
That is just how organic his performance was and that he just crushed it.

562
00:26:59.020 --> 00:27:04.040
Well, he's one of those guys who's been a working actor for a very, very long time.

563
00:27:04.260 --> 00:27:10.000
And I feel like he's one of those people where you recognize him immediately from his body of work.

564
00:27:10.080 --> 00:27:10.620
He's a pro.

565
00:27:10.980 --> 00:27:13.540
We got this interesting letter from Jana M.

566
00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:16.060
in Westport County, Mayo, Ireland.

567
00:27:16.460 --> 00:27:17.260
Oh, wow.

568
00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:18.820
We have letters from everywhere.

569
00:27:18.960 --> 00:27:20.160
This is so exciting to me.

570
00:27:20.340 --> 00:27:23.780
You know, we added a feature on the website where you can say where you're writing from.

571
00:27:23.940 --> 00:27:24.940
I love that.

572
00:27:24.940 --> 00:27:29.260
I know, me too, because it's really fun to see how international the show is.

573
00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:29.520
I know.

574
00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:33.580
Well, when we get mail here to Earwolf that I open, I can always see where people are from.

575
00:27:33.700 --> 00:27:35.840
But before in emails, we weren't always sure.

576
00:27:36.240 --> 00:27:37.720
Here is what Jana said.

577
00:27:38.040 --> 00:27:49.280
Fun fact, James Urbaniak, the actor who played Dwight's best friend Rolf, whom he met in a shoe store, also played a shoe store employee with a foot fetish on Sex and the City.

578
00:27:49.920 --> 00:27:53.000
What is it about James Urbaniak in shoe stores?

579
00:27:53.580 --> 00:27:54.600
That's really funny.

580
00:27:54.600 --> 00:27:55.600
I think that's fun.

581
00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:57.460
And now Christine B.

582
00:27:57.740 --> 00:27:59.880
from Mississippi asked this.

583
00:28:00.120 --> 00:28:05.580
I've heard that Rolf was introduced because Moe's was busy on Parks and Rec.

584
00:28:05.780 --> 00:28:06.900
Is that true?

585
00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.040
Oh, savvy question.

586
00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:10.480
It is true.

587
00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:15.880
You guys, originally, Moe's was supposed to come to the picnic with Dwight.

588
00:28:15.880 --> 00:28:21.540
And they called up Mike Schur, who was now running Parks and Rec.

589
00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:28.380
And the week we shot Company Picnic, he was directing an episode of Parks and Rec as well as running the show.

590
00:28:28.780 --> 00:28:30.680
And he was like, you guys, I can't do it.

591
00:28:30.740 --> 00:28:31.940
And I guess they begged him.

592
00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:35.540
Like, Jen and Paul, they were like, please, you have to come be Moe's.

593
00:28:35.540 --> 00:28:38.540
And he's like, you guys, I can't do it.

594
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:41.020
I am running a whole other show now.

595
00:28:41.140 --> 00:28:41.580
Yes.

596
00:28:41.960 --> 00:28:45.160
And then, you know, we're going to have Mike on the show.

597
00:28:45.340 --> 00:28:46.020
I can't wait.

598
00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:50.700
And he's going to tell us a little bit about how he also truly hated playing Moe's.

599
00:28:51.100 --> 00:28:51.820
Hated it.

600
00:28:51.980 --> 00:28:52.680
Hated it.

601
00:28:52.680 --> 00:29:02.720
So I think he was, like, really happy that he had a good excuse to not be out in this field in his wool clothes for four days.

602
00:29:02.920 --> 00:29:07.000
It also made sense to me that Dwight wouldn't have brought Moe's to the Company Picnic.

603
00:29:07.200 --> 00:29:11.460
And I love this twist that he's got this best friend.

604
00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:12.080
Yeah.

605
00:29:12.440 --> 00:29:21.000
You know, there's a deleted talking head that made me laugh, but also sad, where Michael says he usually brings the guy from his condo with him.

606
00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:23.440
But this year, he came by himself.

607
00:29:24.700 --> 00:29:26.540
The guy from his condo.

608
00:29:26.940 --> 00:29:27.420
Yeah.

609
00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:31.880
Well, Rolf is going to appear in four episodes of The Office.

610
00:29:31.920 --> 00:29:33.300
This was his firSt.

611
00:29:33.780 --> 00:29:34.960
We loved you, James.

612
00:29:35.100 --> 00:29:36.520
He was really fun to work with.

613
00:29:36.540 --> 00:29:36.960
So fun.

614
00:29:37.840 --> 00:29:39.480
Now enters Holly.

615
00:29:40.080 --> 00:29:42.200
Oh, and Michael sees her.

616
00:29:42.360 --> 00:29:43.940
And Kevin's like, there's Holly.

617
00:29:44.080 --> 00:29:45.840
And Michael's like, oh, you know, we're just friends.

618
00:29:46.540 --> 00:29:51.100
There's a whole awkward greeting between Holly and her boyfriend, AJ, with Michael.

619
00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:55.040
And Jenna, this begins, snarky Michael.

620
00:29:55.580 --> 00:30:00.860
Steve does this thing as Michael I love so much, where he lets his hatred for someone just barely poke out.

621
00:30:01.100 --> 00:30:01.440
Mm-hmm.

622
00:30:02.040 --> 00:30:05.060
So he says, hey, I could get you guys some lemonade.

623
00:30:05.520 --> 00:30:07.500
Holly says, lemonade sounds great.

624
00:30:07.720 --> 00:30:08.600
Michael goes, okay.

625
00:30:09.120 --> 00:30:11.440
AJ says, I'd love an iced tea, actually.

626
00:30:11.440 --> 00:30:13.560
And Michael goes, you can go to hell.

627
00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:14.880
Just kidding.

628
00:30:15.100 --> 00:30:15.580
Just kidding.

629
00:30:17.520 --> 00:30:19.420
He'll get him the best iced tea in the world.

630
00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:19.760
Yeah.

631
00:30:20.260 --> 00:30:22.680
First of all, Rob Hubel is back as AJ.

632
00:30:22.960 --> 00:30:23.240
Uh-huh.

633
00:30:23.380 --> 00:30:24.540
And he's so good.

634
00:30:24.780 --> 00:30:27.320
He's being so nice to Michael.

635
00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:27.860
I know.

636
00:30:27.980 --> 00:30:28.700
The whole episode.

637
00:30:28.720 --> 00:30:29.420
The whole episode.

638
00:30:29.420 --> 00:30:30.640
And you're like, oh, my gosh.

639
00:30:30.680 --> 00:30:34.880
This guy must really love Holly to be that patient with Michael.

640
00:30:35.180 --> 00:30:38.800
I want to point out in this scene that Kevin is having a beer.

641
00:30:39.220 --> 00:30:39.700
Yes.

642
00:30:39.860 --> 00:30:41.260
Holly asks for a lemonade.

643
00:30:41.260 --> 00:30:43.500
AJ wants an iced tea.

644
00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:48.840
According to a big banner in the background, you can really see it over Michael's shoulder

645
00:30:48.840 --> 00:30:50.440
and his upcoming talking head.

646
00:30:50.640 --> 00:30:55.080
There is a breakdown of everything the Dunder Mifflin Company picnic is serving.

647
00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:55.920
Oh.

648
00:30:56.320 --> 00:31:02.740
Food was hamburgers, turkey burgers, hot dogs, corn on the cob, salads.

649
00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:04.680
Listen to the beverage liSt.

650
00:31:05.260 --> 00:31:05.980
Pina colada.

651
00:31:06.140 --> 00:31:07.240
Charles drinks one of those.

652
00:31:07.600 --> 00:31:08.160
Mai Tai.

653
00:31:08.540 --> 00:31:09.680
Stanley drinks one of those.

654
00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:10.480
Hurricane.

655
00:31:10.480 --> 00:31:10.580
Wine.

656
00:31:10.780 --> 00:31:11.660
Oh, wow.

657
00:31:12.220 --> 00:31:13.380
Tequila sunrise.

658
00:31:13.660 --> 00:31:14.060
Dang.

659
00:31:14.480 --> 00:31:18.040
Beer, wine, sodas, water.

660
00:31:18.420 --> 00:31:19.360
No iced tea.

661
00:31:19.800 --> 00:31:20.660
No lemonade.

662
00:31:22.540 --> 00:31:24.060
Lots of booze.

663
00:31:24.120 --> 00:31:25.320
Lots of booze.

664
00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:30.060
You know, Michael has a talking head where he says, I lied to Kevin.

665
00:31:30.520 --> 00:31:32.320
Holly and I could never just be friends.

666
00:31:32.320 --> 00:31:37.060
And he wrote a whole list of bullet points, why they should be together on like a receipt,

667
00:31:37.320 --> 00:31:38.280
on some kind of receipt.

668
00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:40.260
He didn't use a proper piece of paper.

669
00:31:40.340 --> 00:31:40.620
No.

670
00:31:40.740 --> 00:31:41.900
And he's trying to read it.

671
00:31:42.180 --> 00:31:44.300
And he can't really make out what he wrote.

672
00:31:44.300 --> 00:31:46.020
He said, they're soup snakes.

673
00:31:46.600 --> 00:31:50.280
And then he tries to justify it by being like, I think, okay, yeah.

674
00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:52.460
I think it's because when we have soup.

675
00:31:52.680 --> 00:31:53.000
Mm-hmm.

676
00:31:53.280 --> 00:31:54.320
And then he's like, no, no.

677
00:31:54.700 --> 00:31:55.140
Soulmates.

678
00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:59.080
Well, we had a fan question from Tracy C.

679
00:31:59.300 --> 00:32:01.340
in Georgia who said this,

680
00:32:01.340 --> 00:32:05.320
I have been holding on to this fast fact for so long.

681
00:32:05.480 --> 00:32:07.780
Please include it in this episode.

682
00:32:08.160 --> 00:32:08.920
What is it?

683
00:32:09.380 --> 00:32:16.560
Mindy describes her and BJ's relationship as soup snakes because she loves the scene

684
00:32:16.560 --> 00:32:18.740
where Michael misreads his own handwriting.

685
00:32:18.740 --> 00:32:23.360
And instead of saying that he and Holly are soulmates, he says they are soup snakes.

686
00:32:23.720 --> 00:32:26.060
You guys, this is true.

687
00:32:26.380 --> 00:32:28.680
In Mindy's book, Why Not Me?

688
00:32:29.180 --> 00:32:30.340
Here's what it says.

689
00:32:30.560 --> 00:32:30.840
Quote,

690
00:32:31.340 --> 00:32:32.180
We're soup snakes.

691
00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:34.620
BJ and I are soup snakes.

692
00:32:35.240 --> 00:32:36.620
And then she added,

693
00:32:37.160 --> 00:32:41.260
Soulmates is what you aim for, but soup snakes is what you get sometimes.

694
00:32:41.820 --> 00:32:42.340
Aww.

695
00:32:42.700 --> 00:32:44.160
Is that so sweet?

696
00:32:44.440 --> 00:32:44.780
Yeah.

697
00:32:45.260 --> 00:32:46.280
They are soup snakes.

698
00:32:46.340 --> 00:32:47.500
They are soup snakes.

699
00:32:48.100 --> 00:32:52.940
Pam and Jim are going to say hi to Charles, who right out of the gate says, nice day, huh?

700
00:32:53.240 --> 00:32:54.360
Jim says, yeah.

701
00:32:54.820 --> 00:32:57.680
Charles says, must be nice to get a rest from all your reSt.

702
00:32:57.960 --> 00:32:59.160
And walks away.

703
00:32:59.160 --> 00:33:01.440
I call this petty Charles.

704
00:33:01.860 --> 00:33:06.300
I want you to know Charles was way more snarky in this episode, but a lot of it got deleted.

705
00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:07.020
Oh, no.

706
00:33:07.500 --> 00:33:07.820
Yeah.

707
00:33:08.100 --> 00:33:12.680
Well, Jenny Tan said that when she was kind of going around talking to all the actors, she

708
00:33:12.680 --> 00:33:19.200
said, both Rob Hubel and Idris talked to her about what it was like to have fans hate on

709
00:33:19.200 --> 00:33:19.440
them.

710
00:33:19.680 --> 00:33:20.540
Oh, really?

711
00:33:20.720 --> 00:33:20.960
Yes.

712
00:33:21.120 --> 00:33:23.300
Because Charles was always mean to Jim.

713
00:33:23.480 --> 00:33:29.400
But I have to say, lady, he is not wrong on his read of Jim.

714
00:33:29.400 --> 00:33:33.520
Like, Jim is very charming, but he, I mean-

715
00:33:33.520 --> 00:33:34.400
He slacks off.

716
00:33:34.400 --> 00:33:35.440
He is a slacker.

717
00:33:36.540 --> 00:33:41.460
He gets his work done ultimately, but he could be more ambitious with his time.

718
00:33:41.680 --> 00:33:42.220
Well, yeah.

719
00:33:42.460 --> 00:33:44.180
That comes for him later in life.

720
00:33:44.320 --> 00:33:46.480
He will become more ambitious in later seasons.

721
00:33:46.920 --> 00:33:50.020
All right, lady, it is time to play volleyball.

722
00:33:50.580 --> 00:33:50.840
Yeah.

723
00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:54.020
Dwight is assigning positions to the Scranton team.

724
00:33:54.460 --> 00:33:56.320
Andy is like, bro-me-go.

725
00:33:56.820 --> 00:33:58.640
Put Aaron next to me.

726
00:33:59.080 --> 00:34:02.760
All of Andy's ridiculous sayings, bro-me-go, it's pretty great.

727
00:34:03.160 --> 00:34:04.260
Well, guess what?

728
00:34:04.560 --> 00:34:06.420
The Scranton team is not doing well.

729
00:34:06.560 --> 00:34:06.880
Mm-mm.

730
00:34:07.080 --> 00:34:08.820
Aaron misses the ball.

731
00:34:09.020 --> 00:34:11.260
Andy starts screaming at her, are you blind?

732
00:34:11.740 --> 00:34:18.820
And then he catches himself, and he redirects the question in earnest to the man on the other

733
00:34:18.820 --> 00:34:20.220
side of the net wearing sunglasses.

734
00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:22.480
He's like, no, I'm really, are you blind?

735
00:34:23.160 --> 00:34:23.900
Guess what?

736
00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:27.460
Sunglasses man was played by our very own editor, Dave Rogers.

737
00:34:27.740 --> 00:34:28.060
Yeah.

738
00:34:28.440 --> 00:34:29.860
But the game continues.

739
00:34:30.680 --> 00:34:31.960
Kevin is not great.

740
00:34:32.800 --> 00:34:35.040
Phyllis sits down in the middle of the game.

741
00:34:35.220 --> 00:34:36.560
Ryan is on his cell phone.

742
00:34:36.820 --> 00:34:37.080
Yeah.

743
00:34:37.360 --> 00:34:40.340
And now it's time for Pam to serve.

744
00:34:40.600 --> 00:34:42.720
And Dwight is like condescending.

745
00:34:42.920 --> 00:34:45.900
He's like, are you left-handed or are you right-handed?

746
00:34:46.140 --> 00:34:47.800
Think about how you hold the phone.

747
00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:50.380
And Pam's like, you know what, Dwight, back off.

748
00:34:50.500 --> 00:34:50.860
Mm-hmm.

749
00:34:51.180 --> 00:34:52.020
I got it.

750
00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:54.000
This is sporty Pam.

751
00:34:55.100 --> 00:34:58.000
Oh, she spikes that serve.

752
00:34:58.300 --> 00:34:58.860
She does.

753
00:34:58.860 --> 00:35:03.980
And then she's like, maybe I played a little in junior high and in high school, maybe a

754
00:35:03.980 --> 00:35:04.620
little in college.

