and one of them was because you guys were all terrible.

1270
00:55:23.730 --> 00:55:26.950
And they all three talk about it on the DVD commentary.

1271
00:55:27.270 --> 00:55:28.150
Can we hear that?

1272
00:55:28.650 --> 00:55:33.930
Volleyball is hard to direct, especially with people who don't have a clue how to play.

1273
00:55:34.190 --> 00:55:34.970
Oh, my God.

1274
00:55:34.970 --> 00:55:35.870
I couldn't believe it.

1275
00:55:36.070 --> 00:55:38.650
They were terrible, I will say.

1276
00:55:39.910 --> 00:55:43.190
Corporate, every other team that was playing against them, so much better.

1277
00:55:43.190 --> 00:55:45.690
I don't know why our people were not good volleyball players.

1278
00:55:45.690 --> 00:55:46.370
I was in editing.

1279
00:55:46.630 --> 00:55:50.690
Paul and I were alternating days on the set, and Paul was like, it's going really well,

1280
00:55:50.710 --> 00:55:52.350
but our team is terrible.

1281
00:55:52.690 --> 00:55:53.690
I don't know what to do.

1282
00:55:53.830 --> 00:55:56.170
And I was like, well, maybe the other teams could be made to be worse.

1283
00:55:56.710 --> 00:56:01.870
I know there was one point where I said, I think Scranton was playing Nashua, maybe

1284
00:56:01.870 --> 00:56:03.770
Utica, and I just said, well, let's just play for a while.

1285
00:56:03.870 --> 00:56:05.630
Let's just play some volleyball as we get warmed up.

1286
00:56:05.950 --> 00:56:07.970
And Utica killed us.

1287
00:56:08.290 --> 00:56:11.590
And I could tell looking at our cast, they all looked so sad.

1288
00:56:11.590 --> 00:56:13.570
I thought, this is a terrible idea.

1289
00:56:13.730 --> 00:56:14.870
Let's just go back to the scene.

1290
00:56:15.750 --> 00:56:16.850
Oh, my gosh.

1291
00:56:16.970 --> 00:56:18.550
You guys were the worSt.

1292
00:56:18.730 --> 00:56:20.190
The worst group there.

1293
00:56:20.450 --> 00:56:26.950
Hey, to be fair, the other teams were filled with special business actors, okay?

1294
00:56:27.350 --> 00:56:31.830
So after I listened to the DVD commentary, I thought, oh, I've got to watch Scranton and

1295
00:56:31.830 --> 00:56:32.570
Utica play.

1296
00:56:32.930 --> 00:56:35.550
Ken said that Utica crushed you guys.

1297
00:56:35.670 --> 00:56:39.090
So I went back and watched the episode, and I never saw you guys play Utica.

1298
00:56:39.090 --> 00:56:40.630
It's in the deleted scenes.

1299
00:56:40.850 --> 00:56:41.750
Oh, wow.

1300
00:56:42.050 --> 00:56:42.250
Yeah.

1301
00:56:42.410 --> 00:56:45.510
And it features some major trash-talking Andy.

1302
00:56:46.590 --> 00:56:47.490
Send it back.

1303
00:56:47.750 --> 00:56:48.090
Yeah.

1304
00:56:48.310 --> 00:56:49.350
Send that ball back.

1305
00:56:50.530 --> 00:56:52.070
Don't mess with Scranton.

1306
00:56:52.270 --> 00:56:52.490
No.

1307
00:56:52.630 --> 00:56:52.950
Uh-uh.

1308
00:56:53.250 --> 00:56:53.690
Utica.

1309
00:56:54.030 --> 00:56:55.310
More like you sucks to cuff.

1310
00:56:55.590 --> 00:56:56.470
Who sucks to cuff?

1311
00:56:56.650 --> 00:56:57.570
You sucks to cuff.

1312
00:56:57.710 --> 00:56:58.630
Who sucks to cuff?

1313
00:56:58.730 --> 00:56:59.690
You sucks to cuff.

1314
00:56:59.870 --> 00:57:00.690
Who sucks to cuff?

1315
00:57:00.810 --> 00:57:01.750
You sucks to cuff.

1316
00:57:01.870 --> 00:57:02.110
Ow.

1317
00:57:02.270 --> 00:57:02.730
Oh, ow.

1318
00:57:02.990 --> 00:57:03.250
Ow.

1319
00:57:03.410 --> 00:57:03.630
Sorry.

1320
00:57:05.130 --> 00:57:09.330
Jim comes up to Andy and Dwight, and he's, like, pinching their arms so they stop.

1321
00:57:09.810 --> 00:57:13.310
But, yeah, Andy starts this whole chant about you sucks to cuff.

1322
00:57:13.710 --> 00:57:14.890
Oh, my gosh.

1323
00:57:15.090 --> 00:57:17.490
But in reality, they were crushing us.

1324
00:57:17.570 --> 00:57:17.770
Yeah.

1325
00:57:18.650 --> 00:57:19.790
Oh, I love that.

1326
00:57:21.230 --> 00:57:22.850
Don't mess with Scranton.

1327
00:57:23.290 --> 00:57:24.870
That made me laugh so hard.

1328
00:57:25.650 --> 00:57:29.330
It's time for Michael and Holly's presentation.

1329
00:57:30.110 --> 00:57:31.010
Oh, gosh.

1330
00:57:31.730 --> 00:57:33.850
This is when David says, I have not seen this.

1331
00:57:34.030 --> 00:57:34.310
Oh.

1332
00:57:34.890 --> 00:57:38.230
He announces that they're going to sing a song, and they're like, no, no, no, it's a sketch.

1333
00:57:38.490 --> 00:57:39.290
No, it's a sketch.

1334
00:57:39.830 --> 00:57:42.630
They're like, David, you should already be worried.

1335
00:57:42.870 --> 00:57:43.090
Yeah.

1336
00:57:43.350 --> 00:57:47.210
And then they say, introducing Slumdunder Mifflinair.

1337
00:57:48.450 --> 00:57:52.310
Slumdunder Mifflinair was a hit movie that came out in 2008.

1338
00:57:52.950 --> 00:57:58.570
According to IMDb, and this is a very brief synopsis, this is what it says.

1339
00:57:58.930 --> 00:58:04.290
A Mumbai teenager reflects on his life after being accused of cheating on the Indian version

1340
00:58:04.290 --> 00:58:06.290
of Who Wants to Be a Millionaire?

1341
00:58:06.950 --> 00:58:08.030
Well, I saw this movie.

1342
00:58:08.110 --> 00:58:08.650
It was fantastic.

1343
00:58:08.950 --> 00:58:09.670
Oh, it's so good.

1344
00:58:09.770 --> 00:58:10.250
It's so good.

1345
00:58:10.410 --> 00:58:11.670
Everyone was talking about it.

1346
00:58:11.710 --> 00:58:11.990
Yes.

1347
00:58:12.150 --> 00:58:13.810
It was huge and just a great film.

1348
00:58:13.810 --> 00:58:19.130
It won a gazillion of awards, including the Academy Award for Best Picture in 2009.

1349
00:58:19.670 --> 00:58:25.950
But of all the movies to parody, to tell the story of Robert Dunder and Robert Mifflin

1350
00:58:25.950 --> 00:58:28.590
coming together, no one knows what they're doing.

1351
00:58:28.930 --> 00:58:31.810
Well, they're also going to get some facts wrong.

1352
00:58:32.430 --> 00:58:35.230
Fan catch from KCK in Orlando, Florida.

1353
00:58:35.610 --> 00:58:40.750
In Michael and Holly's sketch, they say that Dunder and Mifflin met in college.

1354
00:58:40.750 --> 00:58:43.830
At Dartmouth, which incidentally is where Mindy went.

1355
00:58:44.070 --> 00:58:49.790
But in Dunder Mifflin Infinity, Robert Mifflin said he knew Dunder through the Rotary Club.

1356
00:58:50.050 --> 00:58:50.490
Mm-hmm.

1357
00:58:50.970 --> 00:58:51.390
Mm-hmm.

1358
00:58:51.650 --> 00:58:52.030
So.

1359
00:58:52.230 --> 00:58:53.090
I caught it too.

1360
00:58:53.470 --> 00:58:53.650
Yeah.

1361
00:58:54.210 --> 00:59:02.330
Ken shared that they really just drove home with the crowd watching to please not react in any way.

1362
00:59:02.690 --> 00:59:03.830
Even the children.

1363
00:59:04.110 --> 00:59:05.370
Don't crack a smile.

1364
00:59:05.670 --> 00:59:06.150
Nothing.

1365
00:59:06.470 --> 00:59:06.810
Mm-hmm.

1366
00:59:06.810 --> 00:59:12.950
And Ken was so happy with how the scene turned out, because everyone really just looks at them

1367
00:59:12.950 --> 00:59:14.210
so deadpan.

1368
00:59:14.730 --> 00:59:19.650
And Ken said that Steve and Amy pulled him aside after the first take, and they were like,

1369
00:59:19.670 --> 00:59:20.890
this feels really uncomfortable.

1370
00:59:21.410 --> 00:59:23.090
This is like so awkward.

1371
00:59:23.310 --> 00:59:25.550
Amy was like, I'm rattled by it.

1372
00:59:25.930 --> 00:59:29.790
Because it truly felt like they were bombing on stage in front of everyone.

1373
00:59:29.790 --> 00:59:37.010
Well, I guess this sketch took like hours to shoot, and in addition to being told not to

1374
00:59:37.010 --> 00:59:42.210
laugh, the extras were not allowed to move from their spots for continuity reasons.

1375
00:59:42.210 --> 00:59:47.130
So we would bring Waters around and things like that, but they had to stay right there.

1376
00:59:47.570 --> 00:59:52.030
And Jenny Tan had this tidbit in her breakdown from her visit.

1377
00:59:52.030 --> 00:59:58.710
But Andy Buckley, who plays David Wallace, would get on the little stage during the breaks,

1378
00:59:59.190 --> 01:00:02.570
and he would entertain the crowd with stories and jokes.

1379
01:00:02.630 --> 01:00:04.350
She said he even sang a song.

1380
01:00:04.610 --> 01:00:05.610
Oh, my gosh.

1381
01:00:05.730 --> 01:00:07.490
But he was like the entertainment.

1382
01:00:07.890 --> 01:00:11.690
And she said it was just like the sweetest, most thoughtful thing.

1383
01:00:11.910 --> 01:00:12.690
And you know what?

1384
01:00:12.770 --> 01:00:14.570
That is Andy Buckley right there.

1385
01:00:14.670 --> 01:00:14.970
Yeah.

1386
01:00:15.110 --> 01:00:16.910
I was like, of course he did that.

1387
01:00:16.990 --> 01:00:17.530
Of course.

1388
01:00:17.790 --> 01:00:18.790
That is so sweet.

1389
01:00:18.990 --> 01:00:19.210
Yeah.

1390
01:00:19.210 --> 01:00:22.110
Well, the only person that's enjoying this is Stanley.

1391
01:00:22.430 --> 01:00:26.970
We have some classic vacation Stanley when he has his cocktail, and he says,

1392
01:00:27.110 --> 01:00:29.610
I usually don't enjoy the theater, but this is delightful.

1393
01:00:30.010 --> 01:00:32.170
I think he's had a few cocktails by this point.

1394
01:00:32.350 --> 01:00:33.250
I guess he has.

1395
01:00:33.490 --> 01:00:36.330
There's a lot of booze being offered at this event.

1396
01:00:38.050 --> 01:00:40.510
Now Michael and Holly are going to do something.

1397
01:00:40.830 --> 01:00:44.410
They're going to announce that the Buffalo Branch is closing.

1398
01:00:44.890 --> 01:00:46.130
And then they take a bow.

1399
01:00:46.670 --> 01:00:48.570
This is news to the Buffalo Branch.

1400
01:00:48.570 --> 01:00:50.430
They are ticked off.

1401
01:00:50.690 --> 01:00:54.610
Well, there are two especially very angry Buffalo Branch employees.

1402
01:00:54.930 --> 01:00:59.270
They were played by Brian Stack and Marla Garland.

1403
01:00:59.510 --> 01:01:03.150
Brian Stack was a writer on Conan, and I've known Marla for years.

1404
01:01:03.150 --> 01:01:04.530
She is just delightful.

1405
01:01:05.090 --> 01:01:09.930
Well, also seated in the front row, who's very upset about this branch closing, is Jenny Tan.

1406
01:01:10.270 --> 01:01:10.850
Yes.

1407
01:01:10.850 --> 01:01:19.070
And she revealed that she was in the front row with a real-life husband and wife couple, Dan and Aaron,

1408
01:01:19.350 --> 01:01:22.610
who were booked together to play extras on this episode.

1409
01:01:22.810 --> 01:01:24.250
They gave them two fake babies.

1410
01:01:24.450 --> 01:01:26.010
And it's really great.

1411
01:01:26.170 --> 01:01:29.070
You can see Dan sitting next to Jenny.

1412
01:01:29.070 --> 01:01:35.090
And when Brian Stack, as the angry Buffalo Man, is yelling, he's shushing his baby.

1413
01:01:35.230 --> 01:01:37.410
He's like, shh, shh, shh, shh, shh, shh, shh.

1414
01:01:37.410 --> 01:01:39.330
Don't let the angry man upset you, baby.

1415
01:01:39.450 --> 01:01:41.010
Yes, exactly, exactly.

1416
01:01:42.290 --> 01:01:44.310
David Wallace is furious.

1417
01:01:44.930 --> 01:01:47.830
This is not how he wanted the Buffalo Branch to find out.

1418
01:01:48.070 --> 01:01:52.650
No, he says one little boy just asked him if Daddy will have his job at Christmas.

1419
01:01:53.070 --> 01:01:56.190
And Michael's like, well, he's just thinking about his own gifts.

1420
01:01:56.310 --> 01:01:57.290
Not helping, Michael.

1421
01:01:58.670 --> 01:02:00.730
The Scranton group huddles up.

1422
01:02:00.830 --> 01:02:02.090
They're over by the picnic tables.

1423
01:02:02.310 --> 01:02:05.470
And Meredith is like, I think we should forfeit the game out of respect.

1424
01:02:05.910 --> 01:02:09.110
And Dwight says people need volleyball now more than ever.

1425
01:02:09.690 --> 01:02:11.050
Oscar agrees with Dwight.

1426
01:02:11.290 --> 01:02:12.610
Now they have this rallying call.

1427
01:02:12.710 --> 01:02:14.150
They want to kick corporate's ass.

1428
01:02:14.310 --> 01:02:16.230
Yeah, and they're doing great.

1429
01:02:16.690 --> 01:02:19.990
Especially Jim, which we get a little bit of.

1430
01:02:20.050 --> 01:02:20.730
Petty Charles.

1431
01:02:20.990 --> 01:02:22.070
Yes, Petty Charles.

1432
01:02:22.170 --> 01:02:22.690
Petty Charles.

1433
01:02:22.870 --> 01:02:25.210
Petty Charles says, look who just woke up.

1434
01:02:25.270 --> 01:02:28.090
And then scores a point and says, I've been up for a while.

1435
01:02:28.430 --> 01:02:32.150
Okay, so now Dwight is going to stand up to Rolf.

1436
01:02:32.570 --> 01:02:33.430
He is.

1437
01:02:33.590 --> 01:02:40.090
And Jenna, I had one of those moments where I think I thought I heard something that's not in the script.

1438
01:02:40.590 --> 01:02:42.030
It's not in the subtitles.

1439
01:02:42.150 --> 01:02:44.070
And I need you to tell me what I heard.

1440
01:02:44.310 --> 01:02:44.570
What?

1441
01:02:44.910 --> 01:02:46.050
Yeah, exactly.

1442
01:02:46.430 --> 01:02:48.250
Kevin says, it's six to six.

1443
01:02:48.430 --> 01:02:49.210
It's a nail biter.

1444
01:02:49.610 --> 01:02:51.490
Angela says, Kevin, no, it's seven to six.

1445
01:02:51.550 --> 01:02:53.130
Or is that too much accounting for you?

1446
01:02:53.650 --> 01:02:55.830
Rolf says, here's an accounting question for you.

1447
01:02:56.030 --> 01:02:58.510
What does one fiance plus one lover equal?

1448
01:02:58.890 --> 01:03:00.130
Answer, one whore.

1449
01:03:00.690 --> 01:03:02.850
Dwight says, okay, knock it off, Rolf.

1450
01:03:03.230 --> 01:03:04.210
Rolf says, what?

1451
01:03:04.390 --> 01:03:06.710
She is sitting here casting aspirations.

1452
01:03:06.710 --> 01:03:08.950
And Dwight goes, Rolfard, please.

1453
01:03:09.610 --> 01:03:13.630
Jenna, I swear I hear Dwight say, Rolfard, please.

1454
01:03:14.270 --> 01:03:17.150
Meaning like Rolfard is Rolf's full name?

1455
01:03:17.350 --> 01:03:17.870
Yes.

1456
01:03:18.490 --> 01:03:20.070
It's not documented anywhere.

1457
01:03:20.070 --> 01:03:21.510
I'm probably just losing it.

1458
01:03:21.710 --> 01:03:22.770
I need you to hear it.

1459
01:03:22.870 --> 01:03:23.490
I'm going to play it.

1460
01:03:23.710 --> 01:03:23.890
Ready?

1461
01:03:24.170 --> 01:03:24.430
Okay.

1462
01:03:30.270 --> 01:03:31.370
Oh, okay.

1463
01:03:32.070 --> 01:03:33.030
Rolfard, please.

1464
01:03:33.030 --> 01:03:34.050
I'm telling you.

1465
01:03:34.170 --> 01:03:34.410
Okay.

1466
01:03:34.630 --> 01:03:36.810
Here's the first thing I need to know is this.

1467
01:03:36.810 --> 01:03:38.070
Is Rolf a name?

1468
01:03:38.330 --> 01:03:39.250
That I don't know.

1469
01:03:39.330 --> 01:03:41.150
Did we make that up or is it a name?

1470
01:03:41.490 --> 01:03:43.370
Is Rolf short for Rolfard?

1471
01:03:43.970 --> 01:03:47.090
Well, there's a restaurant in Manhattan called Rolf's.

1472
01:03:47.310 --> 01:03:48.770
It's in Gramercy Park.

1473
01:03:49.410 --> 01:03:51.110
Oh, here we go.

1474
01:03:51.230 --> 01:03:51.710
Wikipedia.

1475
01:03:52.150 --> 01:03:52.790
Rolf.

1476
01:03:53.050 --> 01:03:55.310
It is a male given name and surname.

1477
01:03:55.650 --> 01:03:59.490
It originates in the Germanic name Hrolf.

1478
01:04:00.030 --> 01:04:00.670
Interesting.

1479
01:04:01.190 --> 01:04:03.130
But now Rolfard.

1480
01:04:04.130 --> 01:04:04.770
Rolfard.

1481
01:04:05.970 --> 01:04:08.710
We need background music for ladies who Google.

1482
01:04:08.950 --> 01:04:09.930
We really do.

1483
01:04:10.250 --> 01:04:11.730
Booty, booty, booty.

1484
01:04:11.750 --> 01:04:12.050
Okay.

1485
01:04:12.050 --> 01:04:16.790
I will tell you, there is the Rolfard Leather Company in the UK.

1486
01:04:16.790 --> 01:04:19.530
They are a supplier of fine quality leathers.

1487
01:04:19.870 --> 01:04:26.750
Also, just from Ancestry.com, Michigan had the highest population of Rolfard families in 1880.

1488
01:04:27.050 --> 01:04:29.430
So I think you might be right.

1489
01:04:29.730 --> 01:04:31.470
Both names seem to be names.

1490
01:04:31.810 --> 01:04:32.790
I mean, just come on.

1491
01:04:33.050 --> 01:04:38.090
I think you're right.

1492
01:04:38.090 --> 01:04:41.130
I think we have broken a big case here.

1493
01:04:41.510 --> 01:04:44.130
Mom detectives, we declare Rolfard.

1494
01:04:44.370 --> 01:04:45.550
Put it on your calendar.

1495
01:04:46.090 --> 01:04:48.950
This is the first time Rolfard is being documented?

1496
01:04:49.270 --> 01:04:49.630
Yes.

1497
01:04:50.130 --> 01:04:51.670
In the office canon.

1498
01:04:52.590 --> 01:04:53.070
Angela.

1499
01:04:53.150 --> 01:04:53.970
I'm clapping for myself.

1500
01:04:53.970 --> 01:04:54.830
Applause for you.

1501
01:04:55.190 --> 01:04:55.670
Thank you.

1502
01:04:55.850 --> 01:04:56.670
Good work.

1503
01:04:56.850 --> 01:04:57.230
Thank you.

1504
01:04:57.390 --> 01:04:59.450
And now to whoever does subtitles, change it to Rolfard.

1505
01:04:59.530 --> 01:05:00.170
Thank you very much.

1506
01:05:00.170 --> 01:05:05.230
I'd like to say that that was a combo mom, detective, two ladies who Google move.

1507
01:05:05.430 --> 01:05:08.150
Do you see how both of those came together?

1508
01:05:08.830 --> 01:05:09.930
It's beautiful, really.

1509
01:05:10.050 --> 01:05:10.630
In that moment.

1510
01:05:10.770 --> 01:05:11.090
I do.

1511
01:05:11.250 --> 01:05:11.950
I'm proud of us.

1512
01:05:12.670 --> 01:05:16.710
Ken shared that he really liked seeing Dwight softening to Angela.

1513
01:05:17.610 --> 01:05:19.290
Angela's clearly moved by this.

1514
01:05:19.290 --> 01:05:23.110
And then, right after the scene, there would have been an Angela talking head.

1515
01:05:23.270 --> 01:05:25.250
It got deleted, but I wanted you to hear it.

1516
01:05:26.050 --> 01:05:29.430
Today, for the first time in months, Dwight nodded at me.

1517
01:05:30.170 --> 01:05:34.810
And I have to admit, it made my heart sit up just a little straighter in its chair.

1518
01:05:35.210 --> 01:05:40.590
I know I seem hard and cold on the outside, but on the inside, I'm as warm as porcelain.

1519
01:05:40.590 --> 01:05:44.580
And I'm sorry for gushing on like this.

1520
01:05:45.980 --> 01:05:48.980
It just must be the apple juice talking or...

1521
01:05:48.980 --> 01:05:49.360
I don't.

1522
01:05:51.880 --> 01:05:52.960
It's very sweet.

1523
01:05:53.560 --> 01:05:56.480
She is as soft as porcelain on the inside.

1524
01:05:57.400 --> 01:05:59.320
Apple juice is not on the drink menu.

1525
01:05:59.320 --> 01:06:00.560
I knew you were going to say that.

1526
01:06:00.840 --> 01:06:03.200
I also now like this expression of saying,

1527
01:06:03.340 --> 01:06:06.240
it just made my heart sit up a little straighter in its chair.

1528
01:06:06.240 --> 01:06:07.220
I loved that too.

1529
01:06:07.220 --> 01:06:08.420
I thought it was cute.

1530
01:06:08.620 --> 01:06:08.920
What?

1531
01:06:08.920 --> 01:06:13.740
The game is going and Pam is going to fall.

1532
01:06:14.400 --> 01:06:16.120
Lady, I did my own falling stunt.

1533
01:06:16.280 --> 01:06:16.780
That's all me.

1534
01:06:17.000 --> 01:06:17.980
I believed it.

1535
01:06:18.080 --> 01:06:18.900
I'm very proud of it.

1536
01:06:19.060 --> 01:06:21.540
It's not the first time you fall in this episode.

1537
01:06:21.540 --> 01:06:22.520
You fall twice.

1538
01:06:22.700 --> 01:06:23.200
I do?

1539
01:06:23.440 --> 01:06:23.600
Yeah.

1540
01:06:23.840 --> 01:06:29.780
You had a spontaneous fall while you were playing fake volleyball earlier in the episode.

1541
01:06:29.940 --> 01:06:30.300
Oh.

1542
01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:31.260
I clocked it.

1543
01:06:31.360 --> 01:06:33.220
You went down to your knees to get a ball.

1544
01:06:33.580 --> 01:06:33.960
Huh.

1545
01:06:34.200 --> 01:06:34.540
Mm-hmm.

1546
01:06:34.800 --> 01:06:35.700
I'm a pro.

1547
01:06:35.920 --> 01:06:37.240
You are sporty, Pam.

1548
01:06:38.000 --> 01:06:42.540
Well, there had been a lot of discussion about using my double and shooting the fall from

1549
01:06:42.540 --> 01:06:47.480
behind, but Ken said to sell it, they really needed to see my face on camera.

1550
01:06:47.640 --> 01:06:49.360
And it wasn't the shoulder rotation.

1551
01:06:49.800 --> 01:06:50.320
Yes.

1552
01:06:50.380 --> 01:06:52.820
There was no reason why they couldn't just have me fall.

1553
01:06:53.000 --> 01:06:54.740
It was not going to affect my shoulder.

1554
01:06:55.540 --> 01:07:02.520
Randy told me that sometimes in movies, they will use a stunt double from the front and then

1555
01:07:02.520 --> 01:07:04.720
they do CGI face replacement.

1556
01:07:05.040 --> 01:07:05.380
What?

1557
01:07:05.640 --> 01:07:05.800
Yeah.

1558
01:07:05.800 --> 01:07:07.120
Is this face-off?

1559
01:07:07.380 --> 01:07:08.100
Kind of.

1560
01:07:08.220 --> 01:07:10.480
Like the movie magic version of face-off.

1561
01:07:10.640 --> 01:07:12.400
He said, we could not afford that.

1562
01:07:12.780 --> 01:07:16.140
So there was no putting my face on her face.

1563
01:07:16.600 --> 01:07:16.840
Okay.

1564
01:07:17.220 --> 01:07:22.720
So you know, at the end of this, when Pam is going to leave to get her ankle checked,

1565
01:07:23.300 --> 01:07:25.340
Dwight has to start stalling for time.

1566
01:07:25.360 --> 01:07:29.180
And the first thing he does is he like kicks a volleyball really far away.

1567
01:07:29.180 --> 01:07:35.160
This reminded me of like the butthole kid growing up, like when you played kickball, who would

1568
01:07:35.160 --> 01:07:37.300
have a tantrum and kick the ball real far.

1569
01:07:37.440 --> 01:07:37.780
Totally.

1570
01:07:37.800 --> 01:07:38.880
And someone had to go get it.

1571
01:07:39.060 --> 01:07:41.300
Well, we had a fan catch from Emily H.

1572
01:07:41.400 --> 01:07:43.060
in Ohio who said,

1573
01:07:43.060 --> 01:07:46.880
I have a background catch at 16 minutes, 55 seconds.

1574
01:07:47.120 --> 01:07:53.400
When Dwight kicks the volleyball away to stall the game, there are some weird face cutout board

1575
01:07:53.400 --> 01:07:55.200
picture things in the background.

1576
01:07:55.200 --> 01:07:59.120
And I think there is a person sticking their head through one of them.

1577
01:07:59.440 --> 01:07:59.660
Really?

1578
01:07:59.980 --> 01:08:01.200
I saw those things.

1579
01:08:01.360 --> 01:08:02.760
They look like something from a carnival.

1580
01:08:03.200 --> 01:08:03.640
All right.

1581
01:08:03.780 --> 01:08:10.180
I don't know if this is related, but Jenny Tan wrote this in her diary for the day.

1582
01:08:10.380 --> 01:08:16.220
She said, during the first few takes of Dwight kicking the ball, there was a background performer

1583
01:08:16.220 --> 01:08:17.680
hiding in the shack.

1584
01:08:18.800 --> 01:08:24.180
And whenever the volleyball was kicked near it, this person would wave his arm outside

1585
01:08:24.180 --> 01:08:25.940
the shack and ruin the take.

1586
01:08:26.340 --> 01:08:31.380
She said, needless to say, this person was asked to leave the set and was told not to return

1587
01:08:31.380 --> 01:08:32.520
for the rest of the week.

1588
01:08:32.960 --> 01:08:33.700
I don't know.

1589
01:08:33.800 --> 01:08:34.560
What's happening?

1590
01:08:34.560 --> 01:08:35.400
I don't know.

1591
01:08:35.660 --> 01:08:40.400
I was like, could that be the person whose face was in the little, like, picture thing?

1592
01:08:40.460 --> 01:08:42.160
Well, you know I'm going to go back and look.

1593
01:08:42.300 --> 01:08:42.680
I know.

1594
01:08:43.460 --> 01:08:47.020
Well, not in the shack, waving their arms, or Michael and Holly.

1595
01:08:47.020 --> 01:08:48.120
How's that for a transition?

1596
01:08:48.120 --> 01:08:49.340
That was a wonderful transition.

1597
01:08:49.680 --> 01:08:50.200
I like that.

1598
01:08:50.440 --> 01:08:51.600
We should share with you guys.

1599
01:08:51.600 --> 01:08:53.140
We often wonder how to transition.

1600
01:08:54.380 --> 01:08:58.340
We are trying so hard not to have every transition be lady.

1601
01:08:58.640 --> 01:08:59.740
Lady are well.

1602
01:09:00.120 --> 01:09:00.580
Yes.

1603
01:09:00.760 --> 01:09:01.440
Oh, the wells.

1604
01:09:01.680 --> 01:09:01.980
The wells.

1605
01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:02.780
We do a lot of wells.

1606
01:09:03.060 --> 01:09:05.040
Dr. Peter Thibodeau, please don't count the wells.

1607
01:09:05.160 --> 01:09:05.660
Oh, don't.

1608
01:09:05.860 --> 01:09:09.200
Oh, I have Dr. Thibodeau a few times, and it was staggering.

1609
01:09:09.980 --> 01:09:16.900
Anyways, Michael and Holly are going to reflect on their skit and on their mistake of mentioning

1610
01:09:16.900 --> 01:09:22.260
the buffalo thing, and they have this very sweet couplet of dialogue.

1611
01:09:23.220 --> 01:09:25.500
Holly says, well, I'm glad we did it.

1612
01:09:25.900 --> 01:09:27.120
Michael says, me too.

1613
01:09:27.640 --> 01:09:32.780
And there's a long pause, and he says, we have a lot of good material for next year's

1614
01:09:32.780 --> 01:09:33.120
sketch.

1615
01:09:33.600 --> 01:09:36.780
And she lights up and says, I can't wait.

1616
01:09:37.760 --> 01:09:41.260
Well, this was a really beautiful performance by Steve and Amy.

1617
01:09:41.260 --> 01:09:46.280
Amy, they shared in the DVD that everyone at Video Village, where they were watching the

1618
01:09:46.280 --> 01:09:47.280
playback, was crying.

1619
01:09:47.900 --> 01:09:50.060
They said Jenny was there, Jenny Tan.

1620
01:09:50.260 --> 01:09:50.900
She was crying.

1621
01:09:51.580 --> 01:09:56.940
And then Ken said something I just loved about this scene between Steve and Amy.

1622
01:09:57.060 --> 01:09:59.800
I wrote it down verbatim, and I want to read it to you.

1623
01:10:00.020 --> 01:10:00.200
Okay.

1624
01:10:00.980 --> 01:10:05.820
Ken said, it's the toughest kind of scene because in a way, everything is happening, and nothing

1625
01:10:05.820 --> 01:10:07.440
is happening all at once.

1626
01:10:07.920 --> 01:10:13.280
There's a gigantic shift that takes place, but it's all under the surface, and the challenge

1627
01:10:13.280 --> 01:10:19.860
is to find it over and over again, take after take, as if they've never been there.

1628
01:10:20.320 --> 01:10:20.840
Mm-hmm.

1629
01:10:21.420 --> 01:10:21.860
Yeah.

1630
01:10:22.040 --> 01:10:23.680
I just thought that was really well said.

1631
01:10:23.820 --> 01:10:29.200
Because every time they did it, they had to have that discovery of knowing that something

1632
01:10:29.200 --> 01:10:30.900
just changed for both of them.

1633
01:10:31.260 --> 01:10:32.400
It's a beautiful scene.

1634
01:10:32.560 --> 01:10:32.820
Mm-hmm.

1635
01:10:32.820 --> 01:10:38.040
And then they say goodbye, and then Michael has this fantastic talking head where he says

1636
01:10:38.040 --> 01:10:41.740
he didn't find the perfect moment that day to share those things with her, but it's

1637
01:10:41.740 --> 01:10:46.300
okay because they're going to be one of those couples who have a long story, and he's just

1638
01:10:46.300 --> 01:10:47.140
going to be patient.

1639
01:10:47.780 --> 01:10:47.940
Yeah.

1640
01:10:48.160 --> 01:10:52.880
Jen said in an interview that they loved setting up this idea that Michael was going to find

1641
01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:56.320
a way at this picnic to try to make his move with Holly.

1642
01:10:56.640 --> 01:11:02.740
But then, over the course of the day, as he spent time with her, he was reminded that

1643
01:11:02.740 --> 01:11:07.660
they have something really special, and he gains this more mature way of looking at

1644
01:11:07.660 --> 01:11:13.400
the relationship, and it's very different than how he would behave if this were Jan or

1645
01:11:13.400 --> 01:11:20.720
any other woman from his past, and that she said, quote, he was calm and confident and

1646
01:11:20.720 --> 01:11:22.380
quieted by this thought.

1647
01:11:22.380 --> 01:11:24.160
And I loved that.

1648
01:11:24.360 --> 01:11:24.720
Mm-hmm.

1649
01:11:24.880 --> 01:11:31.300
And this talking head right here is why you know this is his soup snake.

1650
01:11:31.820 --> 01:11:32.320
Yeah.

1651
01:11:32.640 --> 01:11:33.580
His soulmate.

1652
01:11:35.060 --> 01:11:36.700
A hundred percent, right?

1653
01:11:37.220 --> 01:11:37.640
Yeah.

1654
01:11:37.960 --> 01:11:46.260
Well, Jim is going to take Pam to a local hospital, and for whatever reason, they have this belief

1655
01:11:46.260 --> 01:11:48.840
that Dwight can stall this volleyball game.

1656
01:11:48.840 --> 01:11:49.740
I mean...

1657
01:11:49.740 --> 01:11:50.520
For how long?

1658
01:11:50.580 --> 01:11:51.420
I mean, you...

1659
01:11:51.420 --> 01:11:55.100
Have you ever gone to get an ankle checked or anything checked?

1660
01:11:55.100 --> 01:11:55.500
Anything.

1661
01:11:55.720 --> 01:12:00.160
Even just the commute and finding parking and getting inside and signing up and getting

1662
01:12:00.160 --> 01:12:02.300
your insurance information and...

1663
01:12:02.300 --> 01:12:03.000
I don't know.

1664
01:12:03.340 --> 01:12:09.380
Jim is feverishly filling out some hospital form while a sassy nurse is wheeling Pam away.

1665
01:12:10.120 --> 01:12:12.380
The sassy nurse was played by Allison Martin.

1666
01:12:12.700 --> 01:12:18.080
She's done a ton of television comedy, most recently Grace and Frankie, and she did an episode

1667
01:12:18.840 --> 01:12:19.260
Oh.

1668
01:12:19.580 --> 01:12:21.660
We had a fan question from Christy H.

1669
01:12:21.720 --> 01:12:22.780
in Maryland who said,

1670
01:12:22.940 --> 01:12:27.340
My 13-year-old son thinks the hospital that Jim and Pam go to is the Scrubs Hospital.

1671
01:12:27.360 --> 01:12:28.260
Is he right?

1672
01:12:28.260 --> 01:12:29.600
He's a huge Office fan.

1673
01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:31.100
And Sam O.

1674
01:12:31.300 --> 01:12:32.960
from Milwaukee, Wisconsin said,

1675
01:12:33.200 --> 01:12:37.720
At the end of this episode, you guys are clearly in the hospital from Scrubs.

1676
01:12:37.960 --> 01:12:40.080
Do you remember anything about working there?

1677
01:12:40.240 --> 01:12:42.420
Was the cast of the other show around at all?

1678
01:12:42.600 --> 01:12:43.840
Well, I tell you what.

1679
01:12:44.000 --> 01:12:45.380
Christy, your son is right.

1680
01:12:46.060 --> 01:12:47.260
Sam, you are right.

1681
01:12:47.260 --> 01:12:52.060
This was the hospital that they used on Scrubs.

1682
01:12:52.660 --> 01:12:54.260
It is a former hospital.

1683
01:12:54.420 --> 01:12:55.660
It's not even around anymore.

1684
01:12:55.880 --> 01:12:56.720
They've torn it down.

1685
01:12:56.860 --> 01:12:59.420
But at the time, it was an abandoned hospital.

1686
01:12:59.420 --> 01:13:02.400
It was the Riverside Community Hospital in Sherman Oaks.

1687
01:13:02.660 --> 01:13:04.980
The Scrubs cast were not there that day.

1688
01:13:05.160 --> 01:13:11.720
But Randy told us that their production graciously allowed us to use some of their pre-dressed corridors

1689
01:13:11.720 --> 01:13:13.200
and examination rooMs.

1690
01:13:13.500 --> 01:13:19.500
And something I'll tell you is that we shot all of this hospital stuff on Monday.

1691
01:13:19.500 --> 01:13:21.540
It was our very first day of shooting.

1692
01:13:21.660 --> 01:13:24.240
It was before we ever went out to the company picnic.

1693
01:13:24.560 --> 01:13:28.140
So all of that emotion was just day one.

1694
01:13:28.260 --> 01:13:28.700
Day one.

1695
01:13:28.880 --> 01:13:29.080
Wow.

1696
01:13:29.080 --> 01:13:32.800
We started with the cold open, and then we relocated to the hospital.

1697
01:13:33.320 --> 01:13:38.640
And Jenny recalled that she was not allowed to observe the hospital.

1698
01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:42.100
She knew that we were going to a hospital, but she didn't know why.

1699
01:13:42.260 --> 01:13:44.680
And we'll tell you more about that in just a little bit.

1700
01:13:45.020 --> 01:13:47.080
I don't know how much longer Dwight can stall.

1701
01:13:47.300 --> 01:13:50.720
The corporate team is insisting that Scranton put in their subs.

1702
01:13:50.720 --> 01:13:54.340
And Dwight is doing this really long roundabout thing of like,

1703
01:13:54.400 --> 01:13:56.960
well, how many people must get hurt before a lesson is learned?

1704
01:13:57.120 --> 01:14:01.600
One, two, three, four.

1705
01:14:01.920 --> 01:14:04.220
He's doing a horrible job of stalling.

1706
01:14:04.460 --> 01:14:06.520
But Jim is like, Dwight, keep stalling.

1707
01:14:06.640 --> 01:14:09.820
And then he gets called into the room where Pam is.

1708
01:14:10.080 --> 01:14:12.580
And they get some pretty big news.

1709
01:14:12.780 --> 01:14:14.260
But we can't hear it.

1710
01:14:14.500 --> 01:14:14.980
Nope.

1711
01:14:15.260 --> 01:14:16.940
But I think we know what it is.

1712
01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:17.500
Yes.

1713
01:14:17.980 --> 01:14:19.140
We got some mail.

1714
01:14:19.140 --> 01:14:24.340
A lot of people wanted to know, why was this scene silent?

1715
01:14:25.340 --> 01:14:28.100
Obviously, they're being told that they're going to have a baby.

1716
01:14:28.340 --> 01:14:29.500
Why couldn't we hear it?

1717
01:14:30.040 --> 01:14:33.220
Well, this was partially inspired by the British show.

1718
01:14:33.380 --> 01:14:38.520
There is a scene in that series where Tim is going to tell Dawn how he feels about her.

1719
01:14:38.660 --> 01:14:40.600
But first, he takes off his microphone.

1720
01:14:41.060 --> 01:14:46.500
And Jen and Paul thought that this made that moment even more intimate.

1721
01:14:46.500 --> 01:14:49.900
It's one of those things, kind of like the teapot note.

1722
01:14:50.200 --> 01:14:56.900
There's nothing that you could write that could ever meet people's expectations of what

1723
01:14:56.900 --> 01:14:58.060
it needed to be.

1724
01:14:58.240 --> 01:15:03.640
So if you leave it for people to fill in themselves, it'll always be the perfect note.

1725
01:15:03.860 --> 01:15:04.560
I agree.

1726
01:15:04.560 --> 01:15:09.040
And I feel like Randall Einhorn shared with us that the further you were away from a moment,

1727
01:15:09.040 --> 01:15:11.200
the more intimate it feels to watch.

1728
01:15:11.380 --> 01:15:11.840
Yeah.

1729
01:15:12.020 --> 01:15:14.920
And so removing the sound makes you pretty far away.

1730
01:15:15.280 --> 01:15:15.540
Yeah.

1731
01:15:15.880 --> 01:15:19.540
Well, this idea was something we had been toying with for a long time.

1732
01:15:19.720 --> 01:15:24.680
On casino night, there was a whole conversation about whether or not we should hear Jim tell

1733
01:15:24.680 --> 01:15:28.120
Pam that he has feelings for her out in the parking lot.

1734
01:15:28.120 --> 01:15:31.400
We ultimately decided to keep the audio for that.

1735
01:15:31.620 --> 01:15:35.340
But, you know, we're going to do this again when Pam says goodbye to Michael.

1736
01:15:35.780 --> 01:15:40.120
Every once in a while, it was a trick we could use because we were a documentary.

1737
01:15:40.160 --> 01:15:43.600
We could pull the sound and make a really impactful moment.

1738
01:15:44.480 --> 01:15:47.040
So Jim is going to run into the hallway now.

1739
01:15:47.220 --> 01:15:51.480
He's going to call Dwight, and he's going to say, send in the subs.

1740
01:15:51.820 --> 01:15:52.720
We got mail.

1741
01:15:52.720 --> 01:15:54.200
Well, Annette E.

1742
01:15:54.420 --> 01:15:59.220
from Minnesota said, Jim's face when he finds out he's going to be a father

1743
01:15:59.220 --> 01:16:03.800
gives me goosebumps every time he is acting goals in this scene.

1744
01:16:04.220 --> 01:16:05.320
And Abby M.

1745
01:16:05.440 --> 01:16:10.240
from Utah said, what were the directions given to John for when he finds out

1746
01:16:10.240 --> 01:16:11.160
about the baby?

1747
01:16:12.160 --> 01:16:17.980
So, yeah, John Krasinski, man, why he didn't win an Emmy, why you didn't, why the whole

1748
01:16:17.980 --> 01:16:22.460
freaking cast didn't win more awards, because the show is delivering right here.

1749
01:16:23.120 --> 01:16:28.300
Ken shared on the DVD commentary a note that he gave John for this scene, and I thought

1750
01:16:28.300 --> 01:16:28.980
it was great.

1751
01:16:29.180 --> 01:16:30.820
And I want you guys to hear it.

1752
01:16:31.260 --> 01:16:36.800
The one thing I told John to remember is that over the course of this series, he's developed

1753
01:16:36.800 --> 01:16:41.420
a relationship with the documentary camera operator.

1754
01:16:41.620 --> 01:16:47.440
And so when John emerges from the room to make the call to Dwight, something about seeing

1755
01:16:47.440 --> 01:16:52.280
his pal, the cameraman, kind of suddenly got him very choked up.

1756
01:16:52.280 --> 01:16:53.280
Wow, what a great note.

1757
01:16:53.820 --> 01:16:54.340
And it's like, cool.

1758
01:16:54.540 --> 01:16:57.140
Yeah, that told me this look.

1759
01:16:57.420 --> 01:17:01.920
Because we debated whether or not he should be so wrapped up in the moment that he should

1760
01:17:01.920 --> 01:17:02.700
ignore the camera.

1761
01:17:02.840 --> 01:17:04.000
But in fact, it was the opposite.

1762
01:17:04.180 --> 01:17:04.360
This look right there.

1763
01:17:04.740 --> 01:17:09.780
It was almost like, you know, the cameraman has been sharing so much of what's going on

1764
01:17:09.780 --> 01:17:13.700
with Jim that, you know, that it became very important to acknowledge him here.

1765
01:17:14.900 --> 01:17:18.780
